press your answer as a common fraction. [asy]\nimport olympiad; import geometry; size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));\nfilldraw(arc((6,0),6,0,180)--cycle);\nfilldraw(arc((3,0),3,0,180)--cycle,fillpen=white); filldraw(arc((8,0),2,0,180)--cycle,fillpen=white); filldraw(arc((11,0),1,0,180)--cycle,fillpen=white);\nlabel(\"$A$\",(12,0),S); label(\"$B$\",(10,0),S); label(\"$C$\",(6,0),S); label(\"$D$\",(0,0),S);\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"fb8d58c2b8d770c61a8206284ac6247f7884ec57afd574ad5fb7560782d7deb1"},"seconds":38.535441637039185,"seed":434226688075033383,"stop":"eos","text":"Let the lengths of \\(AB\\), \\(BC\\), and \\(CD\\) be \\(x\\), \\(2x\\), and \\(3x\\) respectively. Therefore, the length of \\(AD\\) is \\(x + 2x + 3x = 6x\\).\n\nThe diameters of the semi-circles are \\(6x\\), \\(4x\\), \\(2x\\), and \\(x\\) respectively. The areas of the semi-circles are proportional to the square of their diameters. The area of a semi-circle with diameter \\(d\\) is \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\pi \\left(\\frac{d}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{\\pi d^2}{8}\\).\n\nThus, the area of the semi-circle with diameter \\(6x\\) is:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\pi (6x)^2}{8} = \\frac{36\\pi x^2}{8} = \\frac{9\\pi x^2}{2}.\n\\]\n\nThe area of the semi-circle with diameter \\(4x\\) is:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\pi (4x)^2}{8} = \\frac{16\\pi x^2}{8} = 2\\pi x^2.\n\\]\n\nThe area of the semi-circle with diameter \\(2x\\) is:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\pi (2x)^2}{8} = \\frac{4\\pi x^2}{8} = \\frac{\\pi x^2}{2}.\n\\]\n\nThe area of the semi-circle with diameter \\(x\\) is:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\pi (x)^2}{8} = \\frac{\\pi x^2}{8}.\n\\]\n\nThe total area of the unshaded regions (the two smaller semi-circles with diameters \\(4x\\) and \\(2x\\)) is:\n\\[\n2\\pi x^2 + \\frac{\\pi x^2}{2} = \\frac{4\\pi x^2 + \\pi x^2}{2} = \\frac{5\\pi x^2}{2}.\n\\]\n\nThe area of the shaded region is the area of the largest semi-circle minus the area of the unshaded regions:\n\\[\n\\frac{9\\pi x^2}{2} - \\frac{5\\pi x^2}{2} = \\frac{4\\pi x^2}{2} = 2\\pi x^2.\n\\]\n\nThe ratio of the shaded area to the unshaded area is:\n\\[\n\\frac{2\\pi x^2}{\\frac{5\\pi x^2}{2}} = \\frac{2\\pi x^2 \\cdot 2}{5\\pi x^2} = \\frac{4}{5}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the ratio of the shaded area to the unshaded area is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{4}{5}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{4}{5}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
